        "description": "Curly hair and sunrise color are a perfect match because each curl becomes a tiny canvas for different tones. With the right technique, you can have warm copper on some spirals, golden blonde on others, and peach or rose on a few highlighted sections. The result is a halo-like effect that looks especially beautiful under natural light. Because curls naturally reflect less light than straight hair, adding sunrise tones helps bring out shine and dimension. Ask your stylist to work with your curl pattern, placing lighter pieces on curls that frame your face and sit on top layers. For care, prioritize moisture and definition with sulfate-free cleansers, rich conditioners, and curl creams. Avoid over-lightening fragile curls; bonds-building treatments and regular trims are essential to maintain healthy, springy texture alongside the sunrise color.",
