        "title": "Sunrise Highlights On Natural Hair",
        "image": "/images/doc_b20_7_img_17.jpg",
        "description": "If you wear your natural coils or curls, sunrise highlights can add luminous warmth without sacrificing your texture or overall health. This approach focuses on adding small, strategically placed highlights in shades of copper, honey, and warm gold that complement your base color. Rather than doing a full-head lightening, your colorist may choose a balayage or foiling technique that respects your curl pattern and avoids over-processing. The result is a subtle sunrise glow that appears most clearly when the light hits the top layers and face-framing curls. This color looks beautiful in twist-outs, wash-and-go styles, and braid-outs, because each highlighted curl stands out against the darker base. To maintain hair health, incorporate deep-conditioning treatments, scalp care, and low-heat styling methods. Satin or silk bonnets and pillowcases will help keep both your color and curls looking smooth and frizz-free.",
