        "description": "Golden sunrise brunette hair color is ideal if you prefer something subtle and sophisticated rather than bright fantasy tones. Instead of going blonde or copper all over, you keep a medium brown base and weave in fine golden and amber highlights that mimic the warmth of early morning light. The effect is soft, dimensional, and very flattering on warm or olive skin tones. This color often looks best with a soft layered cut that gives movement, helping the golden strands catch the light. You can ask for micro-highlights and a warm golden gloss to create an overall glow rather than obvious streaks. Maintenance is relatively low, since your base remains close to natural and the highlights are fine and diffused. A shine-boosting serum or oil, plus occasional deep-conditioning treatments, will help your hair look glossy and healthy, enhancing the sunrise feel.",
