        "description": "On a sleek or wavy bob, peach sunrise hair color becomes a bold yet chic statement that frames your face beautifully. The shorter length makes the gradient more concentrated, so you see the shift from deeper peach at the roots to softer pastel ends very clearly. A bob cut is also ideal if you are lightening from a darker shade, because there is less length to bleach and maintain. Ask for a peachy copper base with hints of rose and champagne at the tips, creating a sunrise-inspired fade that looks intentional and polished. This look works especially well with a blunt or slightly textured bob, as the clean lines keep the playful color feeling grown-up. To preserve shine and avoid dryness, incorporate a lightweight hair oil or serum on the ends and avoid washing every day. Heat-styling on a lower setting helps maintain both color and condition.",
