        "image": "/images/doc_b20_12_img_13.jpg",
        "description": "Midnight navy hair color on straight hair delivers a sleek, mirror-like effect that shows off every hint of blue in the formula. When straight strands lie smoothly, the color appears more uniform, giving a glossy sheet of dark navy that looks almost liquid in bright light. This finish works especially well on blunt cuts, long lobs, and sharp one-length styles, where clean lines help emphasize the richness and depth of the shade. To keep straight navy hair looking its best, it is important to limit heat styling, use a heat protectant every time you flat iron or blow-dry, and invest in shine-enhancing serums that also protect color. Regular trims will prevent split ends from dulling the look, and using sulfate-free products helps your midnight navy stay vivid instead of fading toward washed-out blue or muddy tones.",
