        "image": "/images/doc_b20_12_img_16.jpg",
        "description": "Midnight navy hair color on thick hair creates a bold, dramatic statement because the dense strands showcase the depth of the shade so well. Thick hair can easily carry a dark, rich hue without looking sparse, and the added weight of navy-black often enhances the sleekness of long or mid-length cuts. To keep the color from feeling too solid or heavy, many stylists add internal layers or soft texturizing, which lets the navy pigment sit differently on each layer and creates more movement. Techniques like balayage or subtle ombre on thick hair can show off the transition between nearly black roots and more visible navy ends especially nicely in curls or large waves. Since thick hair can be prone to dryness, it is crucial to maintain a routine with hydrating masks, leave-in conditioners, and heat protectants to keep your midnight navy glossy instead of dull or frizzy.",
