        "image": "/images/doc_b20_12_img_6.jpg",
        "description": "Long layered midnight navy hair is perfect if you love dramatic length but still want shape, movement, and visible color dimension. In this look, your hair is cut into cascading layers that help break up the solid dark base, allowing light to bounce off different planes and making the midnight navy tones more noticeable. The layered structure keeps the color from looking flat or one-dimensional, especially when you add loose curls or waves that separate the strands and show both theinky black and subtle blue reflect. This style works well on medium to thick hair because layers remove weight while preserving length, so the navy shade won’t feel overwhelming or too dense around the face. To maintain shine and keep the ends from looking dry, pair your color care routine with regular trims and hydrating masks, focusing on mid-lengths and tips where long hair tends to fray.",
