        "title": "Midnight Navy Hair Color Maintenance Tips",
        "image": "/images/doc_b20_12_img_18.jpg",
        "description": "Keeping midnight navy hair color vibrant comes down to a consistent, color-safe routine tailored to dark blue and navy tones. Start by using sulfate-free shampoo and conditioner designed for color-treated hair, because harsh cleansing agents can strip pigment and cause your navy shade to fade more quickly. Wash with cool or lukewarm water, as hot water opens the cuticle and encourages color molecules to escape. To revive your tone between appointments, consider a blue or navy color-depositing mask or conditioner that adds back pigment while also hydrating your strands. Limit heat styling as much as possible, always apply a heat protectant when you do use tools, and schedule regular gloss or toner sessions with your stylist to keep your midnight navy rich, shiny, and even from roots to ends.",
