        "image": "/images/doc_b20_12_img_15.jpg",
        "description": "Midnight navy hair color can be very effective on fine hair when it is applied thoughtfully to avoid a flat, heavy appearance. Dark solid color can sometimes make fine strands look thinner, but navy-black with subtle tonal shifts gives the illusion of more depth and body. A few soft, slightly lighter navy ribbons or a gentle balayage around the face and crown can help create the sense of volume without sacrificing the overall dark, moody effect. Styling products like lightweight volumizing mousses and root sprays are important here, because they lift the hair away from the scalp so the color reflects more light and doesn’t appear too dense at the roots. Pair your midnight navy shade with regular trims and nourishing yet not overly heavy conditioners so your fine hair stays bouncy, shiny, and easy to style day to day.",
