        "image": "/images/doc_b20_12_img_19.jpg",
        "description": "If you want to try midnight navy hair at home, it is important to choose products designed specifically for dark blue tones and follow directions carefully. Many brands offer semi-permanent or permanent midnight blue shades created for brunettes, which means some natural dark bases can skip bleaching and still see visible navy reflect. Always start with a strand test to preview the result and check for sensitivity, especially if your hair has been previously colored or chemically treated. For permanent options, box dyes labeled midnight blue or midnight navy usually combine black and blue pigments to create that near-black finish with subtle blue undertones. After coloring, switch to a color-protecting routine with gentle shampoos, regular conditioning, and minimal heat to extend the life of your home-applied midnight navy, and see a professional if you later want to lighten or significantly change the shade.",
