        "description": "Choosing midnight navy hair color for medium skin tone is all about finding the right depth and reflect so your complexion looks balanced and bright. Medium skin usually pairs well with both warm and cool tones, but navy-black often looks especially flattering when it leans slightly softer rather than super inky, avoiding an overly harsh contrast. A rich midnight blue that reveals clear blue tones in sunlight can bring out the warmth in medium skin while still reading deep and sophisticated indoors. You can also add subtle navy balayage or face-framing pieces instead of one flat shade, which helps prevent your features from being overwhelmed by a single block of dark color. Talk with your colorist about keeping some dimension through the mids and ends so your skin tone looks luminous, and maintain your shade at home with color-safe products chosen for color-treated hair.",
