        "image": "/images/doc_b20_12_img_3.jpg",
        "description": "Midnight navy ombre hair color gives you a dramatic fade from dark roots to deep navy ends that feels bold but still chic. The look usually starts with black or deep brown at the roots, then transitions through blue-black mids into more vibrant navy toward the tips, so the color intensity builds gradually as the eye moves downward. Ombre works especially well on medium to long hair because the extra length gives more space for a soft blend between shades, keeping the finish smooth instead of blocky. When styled in loose waves or curls, the gradient shows off its dimension, with darker sections adding shadow while the lighter navy pieces catch and reflect the light. Since the roots remain close to your natural shade, you can stretch time between salon visits and focus on refreshing only the lower sections with toner or semi-permanent navy dye as the color fades.",
