    "heroImage": "/images/doc_b19_8_img_7.jpg",
    "intro": "Rave nights call for hair that looks bold, fun, and stays put while you dance. In this guide, you’ll find 20 crowd‑favorite rave hairstyles for women that mix color, braids, volume, and sparkle in ways that actually work in real life, not just in photos. These looks are inspired by current festival and rave trends likeneon braids, Y2K space buns, glitter roots, and high‑impact ponytails, and they work on a range of hair types, lengths, and textures. Each section focuses on a complete hairstyle look, so you can picture exactly how it will frame your face, what products to use, and how it will hold up through hours of dancing. You’ll also find simple styling tips, maintenance advice, and ideas on how to adjust each look for short, medium, or long hair without needing pro‑level skills. Whether you go full neon, subtle shimmer, or protective braids, there’s a rave‑ready option here that can match your outfit, the venue, and your personal comfort level.",
    "introParagraphs": [
      "Rave nights call for hair that looks bold, fun, and stays put while you dance. In this guide, you’ll find 20 crowd‑favorite rave hairstyles for women that mix color, braids, volume, and sparkle in ways that actually work in real life, not just in photos. These looks are inspired by current festival and rave trends likeneon braids, Y2K space buns, glitter roots, and high‑impact ponytails, and they work on a range of hair types, lengths, and textures. Each section focuses on a complete hairstyle look, so you can picture exactly how it will frame your face, what products to use, and how it will hold up through hours of dancing. You’ll also find simple styling tips, maintenance advice, and ideas on how to adjust each look for short, medium, or long hair without needing pro‑level skills. Whether you go full neon, subtle shimmer, or protective braids, there’s a rave‑ready option here that can match your outfit, the venue, and your personal comfort level.",
      "Space buns with glitter roots are a classic rave hairstyle that instantly says you’re ready to dance all night. This look starts with a center part and two high buns placed on the top sides of your head, which keeps hair off your neck and shows off your makeup. It works especially well on medium to long hair and on straight, wavy, or curly textures because you can leave some texture and volume in the lengths for a playful vibe. To create glitter roots that last, mix cosmetic glitter with hair gel and pat it directly along the part line and around the bun bases using a small brush or your fingers. Use strong‑hold gel or hairspray at the roots to prevent frizz as you sweat, and secure each bun with both hair ties and bobby pins so they don’t slip. For short or fine hair, you can clip in small extensions before twisting the buns to add fullness without weighing your scalp down."
    ],
