        "description": "Mermaid waves with face framing pieces are a softer option for ravers who prefer romantic, flowing hair that still feels intentional. The hair is styled into loose, elongated waves using a large‑barrel iron or waver tool, with shorter front pieces left out or layered to frame the face. This look is especially pretty on long hair but can also work on medium lengths. Adding subtle glitter gel to the front pieces or a few small accessories, like star clips, can push the style into rave territory without making it too bold. It flatters almost every face shape because the front pieces soften the jawline and cheekbones. Use a heat protectant and a salt spray or wave spray to give the hair grip and texture before styling. A flexible‑hold hairspray will help the waves last through hours of moving without making them stiff or crunchy.",
