        "description": "Blonde hair with colorful underlights gives you a peekaboo rainbow effect that you can show off or hide depending on how you style it. The top layers stay mostly blonde, while the hair underneath is dyed in bright shades like turquoise, pink, or purple. When worn straight down, you see just flashes of color as you move, but half‑up or braided rave styles reveal more of the underlayer. This approach is great if you need a more subtle look for work but still want fun color for festivals. Keeping the vibrant section underneath also helps avoid clashing regrowth at the part line. To maintain the brightness, wash with cooler water and sulfate‑free shampoo, and try to separate the blonde from the bright colors when shampooing so they don’t bleed together. Temporary color conditioners are an easy way to refresh the underlights before a big event.",
