        "title": "Braided Pigtails With Hair Tinsel",
        "image": "/images/doc_b19_8_img_3.jpg",
        "description": "Braided pigtails with hair tinsel give a sparkling, playful look that reads very “festival girl” without being too high‑maintenance. You start by parting your hair down the middle and creating two low or mid‑height ponytails, then braiding each into three‑strand braids. Hair tinsel is tied or looped near the roots and woven into the braids so it catches light with every move. This style works on most hair types and is especially good if you want your hair secured but still swinging. Use clear elastics to keep the focus on the color and tinsel instead of the bands. To prevent slippage, anchor the tinsel strands close to the scalp and lightly mist with hairspray after braiding. It’s also an easy look to take down at the end of the night—just snip elastics carefully and slide the tinsel out, then detangle gently with conditioner or leave‑in spray.",
