        "image": "/images/doc_b19_11_img_2.jpg",
        "description": "Wearing a crown made of fresh or faux blossoms remains a quintessential choice for those seeking a romantic and ethereal festival appearance. The key to making this look work is to start with a voluminous base of brushed-out waves that provide enough grip for the headpiece to sit securely. You can use a wide-barrel curling wand to create soft loops, then run your fingers through them to soften the shape. Once the flowers are placed, pull a few face-framing strands forward to create a soft, integrated feel between the hair and the accessory. This combination of botanical elements and flowing hair creates a timeless look that feels both grounded and magical.",
