        "image": "/images/doc_b19_15_img_9.jpg",
        "description": "A Dutch braid crown is a romantic yet sturdy hairstyle that keeps every strand of shoulder-length hair securely in place. Unlike a French braid, a Dutch braid involves crossing strands under each other, which makes the braid sit on top of the hair for a 3D effect. Start at a deep side part and braid along the hairline, wrapping the braid around the back of the head. This “halo” effect is great for outdoor concerts where wind or humidity might otherwise ruin a loose style. It also creates beautiful, heatless waves when you take the braids out the next morning.",
