      "Creating a lived-in texture is the ultimate goal for any outdoor music event where perfection isn’t the priority. Messy beach waves rely on a one-inch curling wand and a generous application of texturizing sea salt spray to mimic a wind-swept look. The key to this hairstyle is leaving the last inch of your ends straight, which prevents the hair from looking too formal or “pageant-like.” You should alternate the direction of your curls to add natural volume and prevent the waves from clumping together into one large ringlet. This style is incredibly forgiving, as the more you dance and sweat, the more authentic and rugged the texture becomes throughout the long concert night."
