    "heroImage": "/images/doc_b14_13_img_11.jpg",
    "intro": "Have you been searching for a hair color that adds warmth, depth, and effortless dimension without going fully red or fully blonde? Warm cinnamon brunette balayage might be exactly what you need. This stunning color technique blends the richness of dark brown withspiced cinnamon tones, creating a sun-kissed, natural finish that flatters almost every skin tone. Balayage remains one of the most requested salon techniques year after year, and when paired with warm cinnamon hues, it delivers a cozy yet polished vibe that works beautifully through every season. Whether your hair is short, long, straight, or curly, this versatile color option can be tailored to suit your natural base and personal taste. Below, we have rounded up twenty gorgeous warm cinnamon brunette balayage looks that will inspire your next salon visit.",
    "introParagraphs": [
      "Have you been searching for a hair color that adds warmth, depth, and effortless dimension without going fully red or fully blonde? Warm cinnamon brunette balayage might be exactly what you need. This stunning color technique blends the richness of dark brown withspiced cinnamon tones, creating a sun-kissed, natural finish that flatters almost every skin tone. Balayage remains one of the most requested salon techniques year after year, and when paired with warm cinnamon hues, it delivers a cozy yet polished vibe that works beautifully through every season. Whether your hair is short, long, straight, or curly, this versatile color option can be tailored to suit your natural base and personal taste. Below, we have rounded up twenty gorgeous warm cinnamon brunette balayage looks that will inspire your next salon visit.",
      "Looking for a way to brighten up deep brown strands without losing that rich, dark foundation? Cinnamon brown balayage on dark brunette hair is one of the most flattering options you can choose. The technique involves hand-painting warm cinnamon tones from the mid-lengths down to the ends, which creates a soft and natural-looking gradient. The lighter cinnamon pieces catch the light in a way that adds movement and body to even the flattest hair textures. This look is especially striking on long, layered cuts where the color transition has room to breathe and show off its full effect. It works well for women who want a low-maintenance color that still feels fresh and modern. The warmth of the cinnamon tones complements olive and warm undertones in the skin beautifully, giving your complexion a healthy, radiant boost without looking overdone."
    ],
