    "excerpt": "Blue hair isn’t just a color choice—it’s a design decision",
    "description": "Blue hair isn’t just a color choice—it’s a design decision\n\nwith attitude and intention. From\n\nsoft gradients to saturated finishes, it has range, personality, and plenty of room for customization\n\n💙 This post breaks down how different blue tones interact with shape, texture, and length.\n\nSmall shifts in placement or finish can\n\ncompletely change the result. Expect real styling insight with a stylist’s eye.\n\nPlus a few moments of humor, because great hair should never feel too serious. A rich blue base flows into lighter, cool-toned ends, finished with soft waves that enhance movement and shine.\n\nThe seamless blend creates depth while maintaining a clean, high-impact finish that photographs beautifully. This airy powder blue shade pairs effortlessly with a layered shag cut, creating softness and natural texture.\n\nThe lightness of the color highlights the feathered layers and gives the style an easy, modern\n\nfeel. A bold electric blue shade brings energy to this textured bob.\n\nSubtle internal layering adds dimension, while the vibrant color placement emphasizes shape and structure without overwhelming the cut. Warm\n\ncopper on the surface conceals a striking blue interior panel, offering a dramatic contrast that reveals itself through movement.\n\nThis technique is ideal for clients who want creative color with professional flexibility. Long, flowing hair is elevated with a saturated teal-blue tone and a refined face frame.\n\nThe color placement keeps brightness through the lengths while maintaining balance and polish around the front. This deep midnight blue shade delivers intense shine and a smooth, reflective finish.\n\nStyled in loose waves, the color reads dimensional and refined, making it an\n\nexcellent choice for long, healthy-looking hair. Multiple blue tones layered with hints of violet create a dimensional effect throughout these waves.\n\nThe strategic color placement enhances texture and gives the hair visual depth from every angle.\n\nA natural brown base is paired with a vivid blue underlayer, offering a creative pop without full commitment.\n\nWhen styled straight or wavy, the contrast appears controlled and intentional.\n\nA sleek short crop becomes striking with a saturated sapphire blue finish. Precise cutting and smooth styling allow the color to take center stage while maintaining a refined silhouette.\n\nThis timeless royal blue shade is styled into soft, uniform waves for a balanced and polished look.\n\nThe consistent tone enhances the wave pattern and delivers a clean, editorial-quality result.\n\nA deep, shadowed blue root transitions smoothly into bright aqua lengths, creating a polished gradient effect. The straight finish highlights precision\n\nblending and keeps the color transition crisp and intentional.\n\nThis short tapered bob features a dark blue base with subtle tonal variation that adds depth without overpowering the shape.\n\nThe structured cut supports easy styling while maintaining a sleek profile. A fully saturated royal blue shade is styled into soft, uniform\n\nwaves for a smooth and dimensional result. The consistent tone enhances shine and movement throughout the mid-lengths and ends.\n\nA vivid blue face frame draws focus forward while deeper blue tones throughout the lengths add contrast and balance. Loose waves enhance separation\n\nand allow the color placement to read clearly from every angle.",
