          "Stylists may concentrate color on\n\nthe very ends and a few surface curls, mimicking natural lightening from the sun\n\nrather than a full salon\n\ntransformation. The result is often\n\ndescribed as “barely there” balayage, where your curls look brighter and more dimensional, but most people wouldn’t guess you had a big color service.",
          "This is perfect if you’re new to color, want to test honey tones, or prefer hair that looks low‑key but polished for everyday life. Maintain it with gentle, sulfate‑free products and an\n\noccasional gloss to keep the honey tone clear and soft, not dull."
